## Change Super Administrator

If a Super Administrator leaves your organization or loses access to their email address, another Super Administrator with a verified email address can transfer administrative ownership.

To prevent administrative lockout, ensure at least one active Super Administrator remains on the account at all times.

### Prerequisites

- An existing Super Administrator with a verified email address  
- The new administrator must be an account member

### Procedure

1. Add a new member to your account.
2. Assign the **Super Administrator** role to the member.
3. Confirm the member has accepted the role and has full administrative access.
4. Remove the previous Super Administrator, if required.

### Outcome

The Super Administrator role is successfully reassigned, ensuring uninterrupted account ownership, governance continuity, and administrative control.
